Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The W-19 receipt machinery existed but M-7's two requirements were unproven/untagged. (1) The gate decision is now extracted as undeclared_failures() and proven end-to-end by a negative test: a fresh unwaived ok:false receipt is flagged by exactly the function the real gate runs; a correctly pinned waiver clears it; a waiver pinned to the WRONG verdict is no waiver (drift fails the gate itself, defense in depth with the waiver-rot test). (2) Every waiver now carries a machine-readable kind from a fixed vocabulary (WAIVER_KINDS/KINDS): superseded, live_blocked, no_verdict_schema, deliberate_falsification, historical_scope_mismatch — with integrity checks (full coverage both directions, known kinds only, kind agrees with the pinned verdict). The deliberate-falsification class — PHASE17C_DISARM_FALSIFICATION, the 19.3 leg-B falsification, the 19.4 ab-pre-repair and diag records — is now identifiable by code and pinned by a test. Receipts themselves untouched (docs/evidence is append-only; the tag lives in the gate table).

Evidence: baseline 4/4 OK with capability probe showing WAIVER_KINDS/undeclared_failures/KINDS absent; pass-after 8/8 OK; run_phase19_gate.receipt_debt_report() re-run against the unchanged WAIVED shape (superseded-historical PASS, current-unresolved KNOWN_OPEN_DEBT, unregistered-failure PASS) — the consumer's 2-tuple unpacking is untouched.

